    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1896-98/document/189> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/420766275/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """I went in to a concert, with Janet –a trio, giving Mozart, Haydn and Beethoven – good music but poor performers. In the evening we read the Bible – Genesis ix-xviii, and laughed over it a great deal. Then I read Placci’s new book of stories,  Mondo Mondano , very vulgar and poor - absolutely  fausse route . 
Sunday Dec. 19. 1897. 
Mr. Arnold Dolmetsch and ‘ Elodie ’, came to lunch, and Janet after, with whom, after the others were gone, we had a gloriously beautiful walk round the Caves. Continued our Genesis in the evening. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 189 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1896-98> .

